# The string pool grows to twice its size plus what is asked for. A size that would not fit in a size_t is "Out of
# memory" (error 512, critical, as a failed realloc already is) instead of wrapping (DIVERGENCES-QB64PE.md D-066).
# On a 64-bit build realloc fails long before; the test is for a 32-bit build, as QB64pe issue 278 asks.
file: internal/c/libqb/src/qbs.cpp
--- old
        oldbase = qbs_data;
        qbs_data_size = qbs_data_size * 2 + bytesrequired;
--- new
        oldbase = qbs_data;
        if (qbs_data_size > (SIZE_MAX - bytesrequired) / 2)
            error(512); // the new size would not fit in a size_t
        qbs_data_size = qbs_data_size * 2 + bytesrequired;
--- end
